       "type": "text",
-      "content": "La ilación lógica es el nexo racional que une dos juicios de modo que el segundo se deduce necesariamente del primero. Los marcadores ilativos como 'por tanto', 'en consecuencia', 'de suerte que' y el clásico 'luego' (con valor deductivo similar al latín *ergo*) estructuran silogismos y razonamientos formales rigurosos sin ambigüedad causal."
+      "content": "You know *por eso* from A2 Unit 5, and *entonces* from A1. This lesson gives you three ways to draw a conclusion.\n\n• *así pues*: \"so\", \"then\". It sums up an argument and starts a new sentence, with a comma after it. It is a little formal.\n• *entonces*: \"so\", \"then\". In conversation it draws a conclusion from what the other person has just said.\n• *de ahí que*: \"that is why\", \"hence\". It points back at a fact you have just stated and says what follows from it.\n\nAfter *de ahí que* the verb is in the subjunctive, in the present or, for the past, in the imperfect (B1 Unit 4). That is the difference from *por eso*, which takes the indicative."
     },
