-          "Habríamos perdido el vuelo matutino, a no ser que hubieras llamado al puerto.",
-          "We would have missed the morning flight, unless you had called the port."
+          "Dijo que vendría a menos que tuviera trabajo.",
+          "He said he would come unless he had work."
         ]
       ]
     },
     {
       "type": "tip",
-      "content": "'A menos que' y 'a no ser que' nunca van seguidas de indicativo. 'Salvo que' y 'excepto que' admiten indicativo solo si se refieren a una excepción factual que ya se sabe cierta o evidente."
+      "content": "The exception does not cancel the rule; it is the single case in which the rule would not hold. If you are not sure which mood to use, check the phrase: *que* means subjunctive, *si* means indicative."
